.TH HTTP_OPEN 3
.SH NAME
http_open \- start an HTTP request with any method
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "int http_open(http* " h ", http_req_t " type ", const char* " location ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_open ()
starts a request of the method
.I type
(GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH or HEAD) to
.IR location ,
an URL or a path on the host of the last request. It resolves the host and
connects. Headers and a body can be added with http_header(3), http_body(3)
and http_chunk(3) until the event loop sends the request.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 on success, 0 on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_get(3), http_post(3)
